{{Term/Store|Dento||Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring character in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|Dento|Game Screen|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Dento|Game Screen|TotK}}</ref>

==Biography==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Dento is a [[Zora]] can be found at his workshop, the [[Hammerhead]], which is located in [[Marot Mart]] in [[Zora's Domain]]. According to the ''[[History of the Zora, Part Four]]'', he made the [[Lightscale Trident]] for [[Mipha]] when she was born,<ref>{{Cite|The celebrate her birth, the smithy Dento presented Mipha with a gift: a mighty spear called the Lightscale Trident.|History of the Zora, Part Four|BotW}}</ref> which he maintains in the present day.<ref>{{Cite|He's the one who fixed Mipha's weapon, the {{Color BotW|Blue|Lightscale Trident}}|Marot|BotW}}</ref> He has two apprentices, [[Fronk]] and [[Ledo]], who he has tasked with making repairs to Zora's Domain.<ref name="Ledo"/>

Like all elder Zora, Dento is initially hostile and untrusting towards [[Link]] due to the loss of Mipha.<ref>{{Cite|So...the Hylian who stole Lady Mipha away thinks he can just come wandering in here like nothing happened. What business do you have here after all these years?!|Dento|BotW}}</ref> When Link speaks to him, Dento is short and curt with his answers.<ref>{{Cite|[What is this place?] The weapons workshop...|Dento|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|[What are you doing?] Trident maintenance...|Dento|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|[A trident?] The {{Color BotW|Blue|Lightscale Trident}} and the {{Color BotW|Blue|ceremonial trident}}...|Dento|BotW}}</ref> Eventually, his annoyance at Link becomes too much, saying there is no reason for him to be there without the Lightscale Trident.<ref>{{Cite|You have been making a racket since you walked in here. There is no point in coming here if you do not possess the {{Color BotW|Blue|Lightscale Trident}}. Leave. Now.|Dento|BotW}}</ref>

After [[Divine Beast Vah Ruta]] is calmed, Dento will be relieved that Mipha can rest in peace.<ref>{{Cite|So I have heard. Hylian Champion Link... Now Lady Mipha's spirit can finally rest in peace.|Dento|BotW}}</ref> He offers to repair both the Lightscale Trident and the [[Ceremonial Trident]] if Link ever breaks them.<ref>{{Cite|As the Champion, you should be able to use both the {{Color BotW|Blue|Lightscale Trident}} and the {{Color BotW|Blue|ceremonial trident}}. If you break either one...please let me know so I can remake it for you.|Dento|BotW}}</ref> Repairing the Lightscale Trident costs a [[Zora Spear]], a [[Diamond]], and five pieces of [[Flint]].<ref>{{Cite|The {{Color BotW|Blue|Lightscale Trident}}... I somehow felt it had disappeared from this world. Shall I remake it for you?|Dento|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|In that case, I will need a {{Color BotW|Blue|Zora Spear}}, {{Color BotW|Red|one}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}}, and {{Color BotW|Red|five pieces}} of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}.|Dento|BotW}}</ref> A new Ceremonial Trident can be made from a Zora Spear and five pieces of Flint.<ref>{{Cite|The {{Color BotW|Blue|ceremonial trident}}... I somehow felt it had disappeared from this world. Shall I remake it for you?|Dento|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|In that case, I will need a {{Color BotW|Blue|Zora spear}} and {{Color BotW|Red|five pieces}} of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}...|Dento|BotW}}</ref>

